# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Environment — SECURITY CONTROL, not housekeeping.
# .env carries the Fernet key that decrypts every client's database password and the
# PostgreSQL superuser password. Committing it is a full compromise of every client
# database (threat T-02-03). Never remove this line.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Backups and database dumps — contain client health data (ordonnances).
/backups/
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Ordonnance photographs — SECURITY CONTROL, not housekeeping.
# A photographed prescription is a named patient's health data under law 09-08. Committed
# once, it is in the history forever: git history is not revocable, and a rewrite does not
# reach the clones. `/media/` is the development storage root (ORDONNANCE_MEDIA_ROOT); the
# test suite writes to a temporary directory instead. Never remove this line.
/media/

# Frontend (web/)
# Dependencies and build output only. Nothing under web/src/api/ is ignored: the
# committed OpenAPI document and its generated types are the diff gate that makes
# "the API contract did not change silently" verifiable (plan 03-10). Adding them
# here would delete that gate.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
